        "fully_constrained": false,
        "notes": "Custom profile L-shape in the XZ plane. IRON RULE 1: sketch local x = world X, sketch local y = world Z. Closed vertex loop: (-25,0) -> (25,0) -> (25,30) -> (20,30) -> (20,5) -> (-25,5) -> back to (-25,0). This is the union of the base arm (world X = -25..+25, Z = 0..5, i.e. BASE_LENGTH_X 50 x THICKNESS_Z 5) and the vertical leg arm (world X = +20..+25, Z = 0..30, i.e. LEG_THICKNESS_X 5 x LEG_TOTAL_HEIGHT_Z 30). Area check: 50*5 + 5*25 = 250 + 125 = 375 mm^2. The single profile is extruded once along Y, so base and leg are one continuous solid (special feature [1], [5], [6], [7]). Plane offset -15 mm along the XZ-plane normal places the section so that the positive extrusion spans world Y = -15..+15 (BASE_WIDTH_Y = 30), centered on the origin."
      }
